WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.867
OUTFRONT tonight.

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.836
We have nukes for that.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.871
That is defeating Naito.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.972
It is a direct threat

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.807
from a Russian commander broadcast

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.576
on Russian state TV.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.311
He says Russia cannot win the war.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.646
He clearly believes it is fighting

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.648
without nukes.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.118
When you a the national resources,

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.021
we realize that our resources, of course,

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.422
have their limits.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.391
And the next spiral of escalation

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.025
can only be

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.194
one nuclear nuke was more of a stimulus.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.430
And we don't have the resources

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.098
to defeat the Naito Block

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.700
with conventional means.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.604
But we have nuclear weapons for that

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.406
defeating the Naito Block

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:40.707
with nuclear weapons

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.441
that commanders

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.842
Cavaliers certainty

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.911
about nuclear weapons is chilling.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:45.979
And it comes

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.181
as the war is now on the verge

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.716
of a dangerous new phase.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.784
CNN is learning

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.119
the United States is now finalizing plans

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.587
to send the most sophisticated

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.623
air defense systems on the planet

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.091
to Ukraine.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.926
We're talking about the US Patriot

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.027
missiles that Ukraine,

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.762
frankly, has been pounding the table

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.165
asking for since the war began.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.332
This system can take down

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.267
tactical ballistic

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.669
missiles, cruise type militia missiles,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.438
aircraft as well.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.772
Now for Russia, Patriot

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.107
missiles have been positioned

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.275
as a red line.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.476
The former Russian president,

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.477
Dmitry Medvedev,

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.011
has warned

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.379
Naito against providing

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.580
Ukraine with them,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:20.947
saying that

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.448
if Naito

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:21.915
did that,

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.650
the Western alliance would immediately

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.251
become a legitimate

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.320
target of Russian armed forces.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.222
Those are powerful words,

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.557
and based on Medvedev's

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.292
words, Putin clearly views

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.360
this move as an escalation.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.628
All of this news

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.764
coming as air raid sirens blared across

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.065
all of Ukraine today.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.835
That familiar, now

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.870
haunting sound as Putin ramps

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.838
up his air assault

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.439
with crucial help

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.541
from his close ally, Belarus.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.609
And tonight,

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.710
there is word of snap

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.678
bell Russian

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.380
military drills along the Ukraine border.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.282
The country's defense ministry

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.617
announcing what it's calling

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.053
a sudden inspection of combat readiness.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.454
The military equipment

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.690
is also on the move in Belarus.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.491
And remember,

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:05.325
it is a country

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.660
where Putin pulls the strings

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.928
just four days ago.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.997
Here he is appearing alongside

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.098
the Belarussian president,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.533
Alexander Lukashenko.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.401
That is at an economic summit.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.536
And now today,

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.770
the Russian military is building

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.305
two river crossings

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.708
along the Ne'eman and rising rivers.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.575
Big question is whether

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.910
this is more saber rattling

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.545
or actually something more

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.080
in light of the escalation.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.815
It is unclear at this hour.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:29.883
But what is clear

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.718
is that Putin's military situation,

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.621
as it is, is growing ever more tenuous.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:35.889
And OUTFRONT now,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.557
Douglas London, former CIA

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.525
counterterror chief

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.393
for South and Southwest Asia.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.394
He's a Russian speaker

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.129
who served with the CIA

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.498
clandestine service for over 30 years.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.200
Tracking KGB agents.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.835
Also with me, retired Army

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.670
General Brigadier General Mark Kimmitt,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.604
who is also a former

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.839
assistant secretary of state

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.941
for political and military affairs.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.242
Thanks so much to both of you.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:56.809
And, General Kimmitt,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.810
let me start with you.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.612
Ukraine fortifying its northern border.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.714
I mean, those are really powerful images

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.016
that Will was able to capture

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.050
of those trenches.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.718
The Belorussian Defense Ministry

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.719
in a terse statement

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.988
announcing these snap military drills.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.890
You've had all these changes

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.691
in the military

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.660
and intelligence structures there.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.029
What do you think this could be?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.465
Well, I certainly don't think

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.734
it's going to be an invasion from Belarus

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.036
the way that the Russians

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.204
invaded from Belarus.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.072
But we didn't think the Russians

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.241
were going to invade either,

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.309
logically,

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.077
because of the size of the Belarus,

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:31.911
an army.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.379
I think the best they can do

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.182
is draw forces away from the south

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.318
and away from the center of Ukraine

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.420
to lighten up the lines

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.121
along the front lines.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.923
I think it's important to remember that

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.858
when the Ukrainians

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.728
did their counterattack during October,

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.697
they actually fainted.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.298
They actually looked like

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.166
they were going

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.534
from the south

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.536
but their main effort was in the north.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.072
So this actually could be a faint

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.108
so that the Russians

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.309
could actually increase

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.744
their fight in the south.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.512
But as for an attack by Belarus,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.413
I just don't see it

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.815
making any sense at all.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.851
So, Doug,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:14.053
the context here, of course, is that

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.788
the clock is ticking. Right.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.057
But the temperatures are below freezing,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.891
well below freezing,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.627
and the clock is ticking and independent

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.095
Russian news outlet.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:22.428
You know,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.297
we were playing that conversation

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.531
a moment ago. Right.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.432
But an independent news

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.166
outlet is reporting

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.501
that the wives of mobilized

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.003
Russian troops are complaining

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.603
and they're complaining

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.971
their husbands are getting really sick

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.373
from the poor conditions

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.774
that they're living under.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:37.110
This case at a Siberian training camp,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.645
they say they're living in tents

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.446
heated by wood burning stoves.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.215
Temperatures are well below zero,

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.916
that any medicine that they have,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.752
they actually brought themselves

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.719
and that they are not

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.854
being properly trained.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.389
I mean, it goes on and on right

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.857
This is in the Bicol time.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.425
So this is in a Russian paper.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.994
And then one of the wives says Douglas.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:55.595
And this is the thing

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.296
that really stuck out

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.263
to me, quote,

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.831
We believe that all this is needed

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.066
for a just cause.

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.601
We are proud of the guys.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.770
We don't blame the authorities.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.338
So even with all this, even with that

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.406
call, we heard

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.909
they take all that anger and frustration,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.578
the absurdity of their situation,

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:13.713
they don't turn on Putin.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.448
What does that tell you?

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.550
Well, good evening, Aaron.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.618
It's not surprising.

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:19.519
It's been consistent

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.753
with what glimpses

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.722
we've seen of Russian society,

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.623
that they'll complain

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:24.991
about the mechanics

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.292
of what's going on in the war.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.394
But they seem to buy into Putin's

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.563
narrative that Ukraine represents

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.831
a significant threat,

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.732
an existential threat,

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.634
perhaps that's Nazi fied.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.269
And you don't really see

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:37.970
a lot of popular disenchantment

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.739
about fighting Ukraine.

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:40.506
You see more

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.307
just complaints

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.142
about how the Russians are fighting it.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.143
And you also see

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:44.911
a great effort

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.112
to deflect any criticism

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.181
directly from Putin.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.682
And putting it on the apparatchiks,

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.352
you know, the bureaucracy, the army,

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.188
which gives him more latitude.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.656
And General Kimmitt,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.257
as Russia continues to bombard

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.492
Ukrainian cities. Right.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.561
You hear those those air raid sirens

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.462
across the country.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.330
Barrages of

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.598
missiles come in now

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.967
with with with some regularity. Here.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.169
CNN is exclusively reporting

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.404
that the Biden administration

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:14.674
is preparing to send those that Patriot

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:15.575
defense system,

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:16.542
the most sophisticated air

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.677
defense systems on the planet.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.412
That is the long range Patriot

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.847
missile system.

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.248
What would that mean

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.583
to Ukraine's ability

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.084
to fight off Russia's air attacks?

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:25.952
Putting aside

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:26.786
that, Russia has said

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:27.653
that that would

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.188
be a legitimate reason

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.190
to target Naito itself by Russia.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.259
What would it do for Ukraine's defenses?

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.828
Well, you do two things.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.496
Number one,

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:38.498
it would significantly alter

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:39.799
the ability of the Russians

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:40.933
to send cruise missiles

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.503
and ballistic missiles into Ukraine.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.938
The more important it would be,

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:46.339
it would

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.574
bolster the civilian population

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.977
inside of Ukraine right now.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.312
Let's be very clear.

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.747
Putin is no longer targeting

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:55.782
in the Ukrainian military.

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:58.217
He's targeting the Ukrainian people,

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:01.254
their infrastructure, their electricity.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.556
He is taking the fight to the people.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.558
So putting the Patriot missiles in

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.894
in my view, is a wise move

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:11.130
because this deflects and mitigates

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.065
but does not eliminate Putin's ability

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.333
to take his word

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.835
to the people inside of Ukraine.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.772
Doug, last night I spoke with

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.040
the recently departed U.S.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.009
ambassador to Russia, John Sullivan.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.744
So this is somebody who

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:26.412
recently saw Putin up close

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.213
or he was in that role

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.147
for more than two years

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.650
under Presidents Trump and Biden.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.352
And he was with Putin directly,

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:35.154
personally in that time.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.023
So I asked him about the speculation

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:39.158
that we all see about Putin's health.

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.660
We're showing pictures of him now.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.994
So you can see a difference

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:42.962
if you just look at a picture

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.430
in the past two years there.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.231
There is a difference.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.532
And the ambassador told me

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.767
that Putin looks,

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.001
quote, puffy

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:50.603
as someone who follows Russia and Putin

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:51.838
so closely.

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:53.673
Do you agree with that?

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.175
You know, it's hard to speculate

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.910
from what we seen outside

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.679
identifying illnesses

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:00.880
and the state of health

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.582
among national leaders,

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:04.016
particularly those of our rivals

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:04.784
like Putin,

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.919
is a major intelligence requirement

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.020
for the community.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.721
And I would tell you,

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:10.990
the CIA has vastly creative

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.925
ways of trying to get tissue samples

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:14.961
and such to try to get a better look.

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:15.761
But otherwise,

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.763
you're extrapolating from open data.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:18.498
And what does it mean?

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:19.398
What are the consequences

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.566
if Putin is ill?

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.668
Does it mean he becomes more desperate?

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.237
Does it mean that we can look forward

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:25.638
to a change in regime?

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:26.772
And would the change regime

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:27.540
be any better?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.107
Any different?

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.141
We're talking about

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:30.243
Putin perhaps

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:32.411
engaging the Belarusians to attack.

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:33.746
Now, here's a country

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.381
that within two years

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:36.549
had protests, marches,

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:38.317
of hundreds of thousands of people.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:39.151
And you'd have to think

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.186
it'd be a pretty desperate act

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:41.687
that could actually reignite

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.289
the fire in Belarus

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:45.758
to set the stage for its opposition,

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.760
largely overseas, to stir

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.729
the emotions of folks in the country,

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:50.863
including its military.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:53.132
So health remains a critical component.

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.667
But even if you know the answers,

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.068
it's what does it mean to you

00:08:58.271 --> 00:08:58.604
All right.

00:08:58.604 --> 00:08:59.739
Thank you both very much.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.107
I appreciate your time tonight.

